      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "This cross-sectional study was carried out on 196 adults (98 men and 98 women), aged between 18 and 91 years."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To examine whether vertebral hemangiomas (VHs) are associated with other spinal pathologies, metabolic diseases, cardiovascular diseases, cancer and past trauma, to shed light on their possible pathophysiology."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "SUMMARY OF BACKGROUND DATA",
          "content": "VHs are the most common form of benign tumors in the spine. Their association with spinal and systemic pathologies has not yet been systematically studied."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Clinical data were gathered from full spine CT scans and medical records."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "VHs were significantly associated with disc lesions (P\u200a=\u200a0.004), past trauma (P\u200a=\u200a0.037), diabetes (χ\u200a=\u200a5.179, P\u200a=\u200a0.023), cardio-vascular diseases (χ\u200a=\u200a8.625, P\u200a=\u200a0.003), and cancer (χ\u200a=\u200a5.820, P\u200a=\u200a0.016), but not with obesity. Only medium-large size VHs were significantly associated with osteoporosis (χ\u200a=\u200a6.695, P\u200a=\u200a0.010)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The pattern of diseases related to VHs suggests a common cause for VH, namely, a disruption of vascular flow in the microvessels (accompanied by endothelium damage) within the vertebral body, eventually resulting in hypervascularization."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "LEVEL OF EVIDENCE",
          "content": 4
        }
      ]},
